From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Atanas Minev <atmin@protonmail.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 21:37:36 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] ci(fork): run upstream's own automation only in upstream
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Pushing a `v0.5.15-s3lite.2` tag to this fork fired upstream's release.yml
(`on: push: tags: v*`), which ran goreleaser and failed trying to publish a
GitHub release to benbjohnson/litestream: "403 Resource not accessible by
integration". Nothing was published — the fork has no such permission — but the
run is noise on every tag the sync workflow will ever cut, and it would be
plainly wrong if it ever succeeded. The fork publishes nothing but its own tags.

Guard the tag- and schedule-triggered upstream workflows on
`github.repository == 'benbjohnson/litestream'`: release, release.docker, and —
because LITESTREAM-FORK.md asks for `s3lite` to become the default branch so the
weekly sync's `schedule` fires — nightly-stability and stale-issues, which would
otherwise start burning CI and commenting on fork issues the moment that happens.

One line each, inert upstream, and it survives a rebase cleanly.
---
 .github/workflows/nightly-stability.yml | 2 ++
 .github/workflows/release.docker.yml    | 2 ++
 .github/workflows/release.yml           | 5 +++++
 .github/workflows/stale-issues.yml      | 2 ++
 4 files changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/nightly-stability.yml b/.github/workflows/nightly-stability.yml
index ca8709e..980218b 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/nightly-stability.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/nightly-stability.yml
@@ -26,6 +26,8 @@ env:
 jobs:
   race-detector-sweep:
     name: Race Detector Sweep
+    # Fork guard, as in release.yml: upstream's own automation runs only upstream.
+    if: github.repository == 'benbjohnson/litestream'
     runs-on: ubuntu-latest
     timeout-minutes: 60
     steps:
diff --git a/.github/workflows/release.docker.yml b/.github/workflows/release.docker.yml
index ad0d189..03a0331 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/release.docker.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/release.docker.yml
@@ -13,6 +13,8 @@ on:
 name: Release (Docker)
 jobs:
   docker:
+    # Fork guard, as in release.yml: the fork publishes nothing but its own tags.
+    if: github.repository == 'benbjohnson/litestream'
     runs-on: ubuntu-latest
     env:
       # CGO cross-compilation supported platforms
diff --git a/.github/workflows/release.yml b/.github/workflows/release.yml
index 6791d9e..768010c 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/release.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/release.yml
@@ -18,6 +18,11 @@ permissions:
 
 jobs:
   goreleaser:
+    # Fork guard: this fork cuts `vX.Y.Z-s3lite.N` tags off the `s3lite` branch, and a
+    # tag push matching `v*` would otherwise run upstream's goreleaser here. It fails
+    # (403 publishing a release to benbjohnson/litestream) and would be wrong if it
+    # ever succeeded — the fork publishes nothing but the tag itself.
+    if: github.repository == 'benbjohnson/litestream'
     runs-on: ubuntu-latest
     steps:
       - name: Checkout
diff --git a/.github/workflows/stale-issues.yml b/.github/workflows/stale-issues.yml
index 2924ac6..10baf32 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/stale-issues.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/stale-issues.yml
@@ -10,6 +10,8 @@ permissions:
 
 jobs:
   stale:
+    # Fork guard, as in release.yml: upstream's own automation runs only upstream.
+    if: github.repository == 'benbjohnson/litestream'
     runs-on: ubuntu-latest
     steps:
       - uses: actions/stale@v9
